## 2. KNOWLEDGE GRAPH SCHEMA

```cypher
// ── Core constraints ──
CREATE CONSTRAINT party_id IF NOT EXISTS FOR (p:Party) REQUIRE p.id IS UNIQUE;
CREATE CONSTRAINT account_id IF NOT EXISTS FOR (a:Account) REQUIRE a.id IS UNIQUE;
CREATE CONSTRAINT txn_id IF NOT EXISTS FOR (t:Transaction) REQUIRE t.id IS UNIQUE;
CREATE CONSTRAINT alert_id IF NOT EXISTS FOR (al:Alert) REQUIRE al.id IS UNIQUE;

// ── Performance indexes ──
CREATE INDEX txn_timestamp IF NOT EXISTS FOR (t:Transaction) ON (t.timestamp);
CREATE INDEX txn_amount IF NOT EXISTS FOR (t:Transaction) ON (t.amount);
CREATE INDEX party_risk IF NOT EXISTS FOR (p:Party) ON (p.risk_score);
CREATE INDEX alert_ts IF NOT EXISTS FOR (al:Alert) ON (al.timestamp);
CREATE INDEX alert_risk IF NOT EXISTS FOR (al:Alert) ON (al.risk_level);

// ── Node taxonomies ──
// Party:  {id, name, type: INDIVIDUAL|COMPANY|TRUST, risk_score:0-100, 
//          jurisdiction, onboarded_date, is_pep:bool, is_sanctioned:bool,
//          corporate_group_id, nominee_director_flag:bool}
// Account:{id, number, type: CHECKING|SAVINGS|BROKERAGE|CRYPTO, currency,
//          opened_date, current_balance, avg_3m_balance, is_closed:bool,
//          mule_risk_score:0-100}
// Transaction:{id, amount, currency, method: WIRE|ACH|CARD|CRYPTO|CASH,
//              timestamp, origin_geo, dest_geo, 
//              velocity_flag:bool, is_sar_flagged:bool,
//              purpose_code}
// Alert:  {id, type: STRUCTURAL|VELOCITY|CYCLE|THRESHOLD|GNN_SCORE,
//          risk_level: LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL, timestamp, reason,
//          analyst_decision: PENDING|CONFIRMED|FALSE_POSITIVE}

// ── Relationships with properties ──
// (p:Party)-[:OWNS {since_date}]->(a:Account)
// (a1:Account)-[:SENDS {timestamp}]->(t:Transaction)
// (t:Transaction)-[:RECEIVES {timestamp}]->(a2:Account)
// (t:Transaction)-[:TRIGGERS {score}]->(al:Alert)
// (p1:Party)-[:RELATED_TO {type:'DIRECTOR|UBO|BENEFICIAL_OWNER|FAMILY|NOMINEE',
//                          ownership_pct:0.0-1.0, since_date}]->(p2:Party)
// (al1:Alert)-[:CORRELATES_WITH {jaccard_similarity}]->(al2:Alert)

// ── GDS projection for GNN training ──
CALL gds.graph.project(
  'aml_fraud_graph',
  ['Party', 'Account'],
  {
    OWNS: {orientation:'UNDIRECTED'},
    SENDS: {orientation:'NATURAL'},
    RECEIVES: {orientation:'NATURAL'},
    RELATED_TO: {orientation:'UNDIRECTED', properties:['type']}
  }
);
```

### Schema Design Rationale
- **Account mule_risk_score** is updated every 5 minutes by the GNN pipeline and provides a single scalar for the compliance dashboard — analysts triage by this score.
- **CORRELATES_WITH** edges between alerts enable alert deduplication and ring stitching. Two alerts that share >30% of the same accounts are linked, reducing the 8,000/month to ~2,500 unique clusters.
- **Transaction.velocity_flag** is a pre-computed boolean set by a streaming query on arrival — if the same sending account has made >30 transfers in 60 minutes, the flag is true, avoiding expensive recalculations.
